**What was observed on the shipped build**
- Entering from Home with no client_id, the patient page's trail, Launch and View Operation links, the debugger, the copied launch link, and the create-case POST all carried demo-demo. Following Launch rendered the case.
- The tenant-less login check returned 400 with no session when signed out, and needsLogin=false when signed in. No 500 in any of six combinations.
- The log had zero missing-relation or NullPointerException lines across the positive and post-restore windows.

**Red check**
- Swapped the parent commit's controller class and a bundle with the two pre-fix components into the running container. Every link carried client_id=null, the debugger showed the missing-relation error, the null Launch link failed with "Unable to authenticate user", and the login check crashed at TenantKey.getOrg.
- Restored both by checksum and bundle hash, restarted, and re-ran every probe green. The signature appears three times in the container log, all inside the red window.

**Automation**
- The fix shipped with LoginControllerTest and PAT-006, which cover nearly everything. One extension to PAT-006 is proposed as write_now for the create-case call, the only affected path the shipped test skips.
- The id tool read the stale primary checkout and handed out PAT-005, which the real spec already uses. I released that reservation; the proposal needs no new id.

